  "result": "`click.KeyValue` is added and working. `@click.option('--set', type=click.KeyValue())` turns `key=value` into a `(key, value)` tuple. Input with no `=` or an empty key fails with `'novalue' is not a valid key=value pair.` and exit code 2. The 8 new tests pass and so does the full test suite.\n\nHow it behaves:\n- It splits on the first `=` only, so `a=b=c` becomes `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`.\n- An empty value is allowed: `a=` becomes `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- If it's given a value that's already a tuple, such as a default, it returns it unchanged.\n- It works with `multiple=True`, so `dict(pairs)` gives you a dict of the pairs.\n\nChanges:\n- **`src/click/types.py`:** the new `KeyValue` class, placed after `UUIDParameterType`.\n- **`src/click/__init__.py`:** exports `KeyValue`.\n- **`docs/api.md`:** added it to the Types section.\n- **`CHANGES.md`:** a changelog entry under the 8.5.0 heading. That section already has a release date, so you may want to move the entry to a new unreleased section.\n- **`tests/test_types.py`:** tests for parsing, errors (`novalue`, `=v`, empty string) and `multiple=True`.\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
